.TH EF2000 6 "2026-11-01" "ef2000" "Games Manual"
.SH NAME
ef2000 \- experimental Linux port of the original EF2000 flight simulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ef2000
.RI [ options ] " _EF2000.EXE"
.B --output
.I DIR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs an externally supplied original DOS executable.
No commercial game data is included.
Each run needs a new diagnostics/output directory;
the original game files remain read-only.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h , " --help"
Show usage.
.TP
.BR \-v , " --version"
Print the version.
.TP
.BR \-f , " --fullscreen"
Start in fullscreen.
.TP
.BR \-w , " --windowed"
Start windowed.
.TP
.BR \-g , " --geometry " WxH
Choose initial window size (default 1280x960).
.TP
.B --aspect-ratio 4:3|native|stretch
Display using CRT 4:3 correction, square pixels, or full-window stretch.
.TP
.B --smooth-scaling
Use linear filtering during framebuffer scaling.
.TP
.B --no-smooth-scaling
Use sharp nearest-neighbour filtering (default).
.TP
.B --data-dir DIR
Find the original game executable in DIR.
.TP
.B --config-dir DIR
Read optional user EF2000.CFG from DIR.
.TP
.B --state-dir DIR
Store native save states in DIR.
.TP
.B --user-data-dir DIR
Override the user data directory.
.TP
.B --cache-dir DIR
Override the cache directory.
.TP
.B --portable
Resolve user directories beneath userdata next to the executable.
.TP
.B --no-save
Disable persistent save-state writes.
.TP
.B --show-paths
Print resolved directories and exit.
.TP
.B --mute
Disable audio.
.TP
.B --no-sound
Disable audio (legacy alias).
.TP
.B --sound off|probe|sb16-probe|sb16
Select sound emulation.
.TP
.B --backend native64|qemu
Choose the execution backend.
.TP
.B --real-mode stop|unicorn
Choose real-mode execution.
.TP
.B --cd-cue FILE
Use a CUE image for experimental CD audio.
.TP
.B --vr off|vfx1
Choose the experimental VR interface.
.TP
.B --controls auto|keyboard|joystick|original
Select flight input configuration.
.TP
.B --joystick auto|off|N
Select an SDL joystick.
.TP
.B --joystick-axes X,Y,Z,R
Remap joystick axes, prefixing indices with a minus sign to invert them.
.TP
.B --headless
Disable the display and write a framebuffer on exit.
.TP
.B --seconds N
Stop after the specified number of seconds.
.TP
.B --check-segment-limit
Run a segment-limit diagnostic.
.TP
.B --runtime-objects DIR
Use precompiled runtime harness objects.
.TP
.B --load-state FILE
Restore a native save-state bundle.
.TP
.B --output DIR
Write run artifacts to DIR; otherwise generate a new cache run directory.
.TP
.BR \-d , " --debug"
Enable verbose logging.
.TP
.B --verbose
Log detailed guest activity.
.PP
Other runtime-specific options are documented by
.BR "ef2000 --help" .
